# BUGS

The `flags` fields of the superblock, a snapshot and an entry are written as 0, or copied, and never read: a volume with other values there mounts as if they were 0.

A key whose type is none of these, in any tree, is kept in order like any other and never read; no check refuses it.
A reader takes inline data at any offset, though a writer makes it only for a whole small file.

Version 1 changed in place in M5 step 10, when a log block's hash came to cover its header; a volume made before then does not mount, and says only that it is damaged.

`docs/11-storage.md` gives the limit on a snapshot's height as 16; it is 32.
It says a create adds a `Kup` only for a directory, and that a removed file's data is cleared in the background; every entry has a `Kup`, and a remove clears the data in its own upserts.
`fs.h` says a delete's key must exist; deleting a key that is not there does nothing.

The superblock's table has room for 677 arenas, but `lib/vx-fs` makes at most 64, and a volume cannot grow.
